----------------------------------------------------------
Exercise Name
----------------------------------------------------------

Spring Data JPA - Quick Example

----------------------------------------------------------
Objective
----------------------------------------------------------

The objective of this exercise is to understand the basic
implementation of Spring Data JPA with Hibernate. The
exercise demonstrates how a Spring Boot application
connects to a MySQL database, maps a Java class to a
database table using JPA annotations, accesses data using
JpaRepository, and retrieves records through the service
layer.

----------------------------------------------------------
Software Used
----------------------------------------------------------

• Java 17
• Spring Boot 3.5.16
• Apache Maven
• Eclipse IDE for Enterprise Java Developers
• MySQL Server 8.0
• MySQL Workbench 8
• Git & GitHub

----------------------------------------------------------
Database Used
----------------------------------------------------------

Database Name : ormlearn

Table Name : country

Sample Records:

IN  -> India
US  -> United States of America

